# Run r1102b slice 5 RERUN, group A config 1 (fresh superflat world, s5_R_setup.md: Boot RA). Rows whose first
# run (perf/runs/r1102b/s5/judged.md) was a batch fault or OPEN for want of a better command; fixes from its
# "Batch fixes" list and the probe fixes in tools/scratch_query/s5_probe.js (getStacks, .nbt, FluidStack from NBT,
# selfloop by recipe type). Mob spawning is off for the whole file except SQ-PSU-04 (crows and slimes disturbed
# the crop rows); every crop row also kills crows and slimes first.
# Order: setup, SQ-PSF-08a (its 600 s wait runs under the next rows, none of which touches randomTickSpeed),
# probe rows, jar, crop clicks, pumps, SQ-PSF-08 read, then the rows at randomTickSpeed 100/300, SQ-PSU-04 (night,
# hard, spawning on) and SQ-FCB-07 last (/reload).
pace 2

## S5RA-00 | setup: home marker, clock, weather, no mob spawning, far site forceload (not a queue row)
bootexpect Done \(
> execute unless entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=s5home] run summon minecraft:marker ~ ~ ~ {Tags:["s5home"]}
sleep 2
> data get entity @e[type=minecraft:marker,tag=s5home,limit=1] Pos
capture S5H entity data: \[(-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d, (-?\d+)\.\d+d\]
> gamerule doDaylightCycle false
> time set noon
> gamerule doWeatherCycle false
> weather clear 1000000
> gamerule doPatrolSpawning false
> gamerule doTraderSpawning false
> gamerule doMobSpawning false
